r).\n   \\]\n\n   The two intersection points are  \n\n   \\[\n   A=\\Bigl(x_{0},y_{0}\\Bigr),\\qquad \n   B=\\Bigl(x_{0},-y_{0}\\Bigr),\n   \\]\n   where  \n\n   \\[\n   x_{0}= \\frac{d^{2}+r^{2}-R^{2}}{2d},\\qquad \n   y_{0}= \\frac{\\sqrt{\\,4d^{2}r^{2}-(d^{2}+r^{2}-R^{2})^{2}\\,}}{2d}>0 .\n   \\]\n\n   The points on the line \\(MN\\) are  \n\n   \\[\n   C=(-r,0),\\qquad D=(d+R,0).\n   \\]\n\n   The circumcenter \\(P\\) of \\(\\triangle ACD\\) is the intersection of the perpendicular bisectors of \\(CD\\) (the vertical line \\(x=\\frac{d+R-r}{2}\\)) and of \\(AC\\); a short computation gives  \n\n   \\[\n   P=\\Bigl(x_{p},y_{p}\\Bigr),\\qquad \n   x_{p}= \\frac{d+R-r}{2},\\qquad \n   y_{p}= -\\frac{(x_{0}+r)^{2}+y_{0}^{2}}{2y_{0}} .\n   \\tag{3}\n   \\]\n\n   The direction vector of the line \\(AP\\) is  \n\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf v =P-A=\\bigl(v_{x},v_{y}\\bigr)\n   =\\Bigl(x_{p}-x_{0},\\,y_{p}-y_{0}\\Bigr).                                   \\tag{4}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Points \\(E\\) and \\(F\\).**  \n   Write a generic point of the line \\(AP\\) as  \n\n   \\[\n   X(t)=A+t\\mathbf v=(x_{0}+tv_{x},\\,y_{0}+tv_{y}) .\n   \\]\n\n   Substituting \\(X(t)\\) into the equation of \\(\\Omega\\) yields  \n\n   \\[\n   (x_{0}+tv_{x})^{2}+(y_{0}+tv_{y})^{2}=r^{2}.\n   \\]\n\n   Because \\(t=0\\) corresponds to the known intersection \\(A\\), the other root is  \n\n   \\[\n   t_{E}= -\\,\\frac{2\\,(x_{0}v_{x}+y_{0}v_{y})}{v_{x}^{2}+v_{y}^{2}} .\n   \\]\n\n   Hence  \n\n   \\[\n   E=X(t_{E}) .\n   \\tag{5}\n   \\]\n\n   Repeating the same computation with the equation of \\(\\Gamma\\) gives  \n\n   \\[\n   t_{F}= -\\,\\frac{2\\bigl((x_{0}-d)v_{x}+y_{0}v_{y}\\bigr)}{v_{x}^{2}+v_{y}^{2}},\\qquad \n   F=X(t_{F}) .\n   \\tag{6}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Orthocenter \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\).**  \n   Since \\(MN\\) is the \\(x\\)-axis, the altitude from \\(P\\) is the vertical line \\(x=x_{p}\\).  \n   The altitude from \\(M\\) is the line through the origin perpendicular to \\(PN\\); its