nt to the circumcircle of }BEF.}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Detailed Solution**\n\nLet the complex plane be identified with \\(\\mathbb C\\).  \nPlace the centre \\(M\\) of the smaller circle \\(\\Omega\\) at the origin and the centre \\(N\\) of the larger circle \\(\\Gamma\\) at the point \\(1\\) on the real axis.  \nDenote the radii by \\(r\\;(0<r<R)\\) and \\(R\\) respectively:\n\n\\[\n\\Omega:\\ |z|=r ,\\qquad \\Gamma:\\ |z-1|=R .\n\\tag{3}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 1.  The intersection points \\(A,B\\)\n\nA point \\(z=x+iy\\) belongs to both circles iff  \n\n\\[\nx^{2}+y^{2}=r^{2},\\qquad (x-1)^{2}+y^{2}=R^{2}.\n\\]\n\nSubtracting gives  \n\n\\[\n2x-1=r^{2}-R^{2}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \nx=\\frac{r^{2}-R^{2}+1}{2}\\;(:=x_{0}).\n\\tag{4}\n\\]\n\nHence  \n\n\\[\ny^{2}=r^{2}-x_{0}^{2}\\;(>0),\\qquad \ny:=\\sqrt{r^{2}-x_{0}^{2}} .\n\\tag{5}\n\\]\n\nWe take  \n\n\\[\nA=x_{0}+iy,\\qquad B=x_{0}-iy .\n\\tag{6}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 2.  Points on the line \\(MN\\)\n\nThe line \\(MN\\) is the real axis.  \nIts second intersection with \\(\\Omega\\) (different from the centre) is the point left of \\(M\\),\n\n\\[\nC=-r .\n\\tag{7}\n\\]\n\nThe second intersection with \\(\\Gamma\\) (right of \\(N\\)) is  \n\n\\[\nD=1+R .\n\\tag{8}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3.  The circumcenter \\(P\\) of \\(\\triangle ACD\\)\n\nBecause \\(C\\) and \\(D\\) are real, the perpendicular bisector of \\(CD\\) is the vertical line  \n\n\\[\n\\Re z = p,\\qquad \np:=\\frac{-r+1+R}{2}= \\frac{R-r+1}{2}.\n\\tag{9}\n\\]\n\nThus \\(P\\) has the form \\(P=p+iq\\) with \\(q>0\\).  \nSince \\(P\\) is equidistant from \\(C\\) and \\(A\\),\n\n\\[\n|P-C|^{2}=|P-A|^{2}.\n\\]\n\nWriting this equality with \\(C=-r\\) and \\(A=x_{0}+iy\\) gives  \n\n\\[\n(p+r)^{2}+q^{2}=(p-x_{0})^{2}