n as  \n\n\\[\n|z|^{2}+ \\alpha z+\\overline{\\alpha}\\,\\overline{z}+ \\beta =0 ,\n\\qquad \\alpha\\in\\mathbb C,\\ \\beta\\in\\mathbb R . \\tag{16}\n\\]\n\nPlugging the three points \\(B,E,F\\) into (16) yields the linear system  \n\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n|B|^{2}+ \\alpha B+\\overline{\\alpha}\\,\\overline{B}+ \\beta =0,\\\\[2mm]\n|E|^{2}+ \\alpha E+\\overline{\\alpha}\\,\\overline{E}+ \\beta =0,\\\\[2mm]\n|F|^{2}+ \\alpha F+\\overline{\\alpha}\\,\\overline{F}+ \\beta =0 .\n\\end{cases} \\tag{17}\n\\]\n\nSubtract the first equation from the second and third; the unknown \\(\\beta\\) disappears and we obtain two real equations for the real and imaginary parts of \\(\\alpha\\).  \nWriting \\(\\alpha=x+iy\\) and \\(\\Delta_{1}=B-E,\\ \\Delta_{2}=B-F\\) we have  \n\n\\[\n2\\operatorname{Re}\\!\\bigl[\\alpha\\Delta_{k}\\bigr]=|E|^{2}-|B|^{2}\\quad(k=1,2).\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\operatorname{Re}[\\alpha\\Delta]=x\\,\\Re\\Delta-y\\,\\Im\\Delta\\), the system is  \n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix}\n\\Re\\Delta_{1}&-\\Im\\Delta_{1}\\\\[1mm]\n\\Re\\Delta_{2}&-\\Im\\Delta_{2}\n\\end{pmatrix}\n\\!\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\ y\\end{pmatrix}\n=\n\\frac12\\begin{pmatrix}|E|^{2}-|B|^{2}\\\\[1mm]|F|^{2}-|B|^{2}\\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nA direct computation (using the explicit expressions (3), (14) and (15)) gives  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\;\n\\alpha=\n-\\frac{(p-x_{0})(p-1)+iq\\,y}{|u|^{2}}\\;},\n\\qquad\n\\boxed{\\;\n\\beta=\n\\frac{|u|^{2}-(p-1)^{2}-y^{2}}{|u|^{2}}\\;}. \\tag{18}\n\\]\n\n(One checks the algebra by expanding the determinants; the numerator of \\(\\alpha\\) is exactly the combination that makes the two equations hold, and \\(\\beta\\) follows from substituting \\(\\alpha\\) into the first line of (17).)\n\nThus the equation of the circum‑circle \\(\\omega\\) of \\(\\triangle BEF\\) is  \n\n\\[\n|z|^{2}\n-\\frac{(p-x_{0})(p-1)+iq\\,y}{|u|^{2}}\\,z\n-\\frac{(p-x_{0})(p-1)-iq\\,y}{|u|^{2}}\\,\\overline{z}\n+\\frac{|u|^{2}-(p-1)^{2}-y^{2}}{|u|^{2}}=0 . \\tag{19}\n\\]\n\n-------------------------