rline{H}\n   +\\frac{|u|^{2}-(p-1)^{2}-y^{2}}{|u|^{2}} .\n\\end{aligned} \\tag{22}\n\\]\n\nWe now show that the discriminant \\(\\Delta=B^{2}-4AC\\) is identically zero.\nAll three coefficients are expressed in terms of the elementary quantities\n\\(p,x_{0},y,q,r,R\\); the only relations among them are the defining\nequations (2), (6) and (7).  Using these relations we simplify each term.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 9.1  Simplifying \\(A\\)\n\n\\(A=|u|^{2}\\) is non‑zero; it will later cancel from the discriminant.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 9.2  Simplifying \\(B\\)\n\nFirst compute  \n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{Re}(\\overline{H}u)=\n\\operatorname{Re}\\!\\bigl[(p+\\tfrac{p(p-1)}{q}i)\\bigl((p-x_{0})+i(q-y)\\bigr)\\bigr]\n= p(p-x_{0})-\\frac{p(p-1)}{q}(q-y).\n\\]\n\nHence  \n\n\\[\n2\\operatorname{Re}(\\overline{H}u)=2p(p-x_{0})-2p(p-1)+\\frac{2p(p-1)}{q}y .\n\\tag{23}\n\\]\n\nNext, using \\(\\displaystyle\\frac{u}{|u|^{2}}=\n\\frac{(p-x_{0})-i(q-y)}{|u|^{2}}\\) we obtain  \n\n\\[\n\\frac{(p-x_{0})(p-1)+iq\\,y}{|u|^{2}}\\,u\n   =\\frac{(p-x_{0})(p-1)+iq\\,y}{|u|^{2}}\\bigl((p-x_{0})+i(q-y)\\bigr)\n\\]\n\\[\n=\\frac{(p-x_{0})(p-1)(p-x_{0})-q\\,y(q-y)}{|u|^{2}}\n   +i\\frac{(p-x_{0})(p-1)(q-y)+q\\,y(p-x_{0})}{|u|^{2}} .\n\\]\n\nIts complex conjugate is obtained by changing the sign of the imaginary part.\nAdding the two expressions cancels the imaginary parts and yields  \n\n\\[\n\\frac{(p-x_{0})(p-1)+iq\\,y}{|u|^{2}}\\,u\n+\\frac{(p-x_{0})(p-1)-iq\\,y}{|u|^{2}}\\,\\overline{u}\n=\n\\frac{2(p-x_{0})(p-1)(p-x_{0})-2q\\,y(q-y)}{|u|^{2}} . \\tag{24}\n\\]\n\nNow substitute (23) and (24) into the formula for \\(B\\).  After a straightforward\nalgebraic manipulation, and using the relation (7) that expresses \\(q\\) in\nterms of \\(p,x_{0},y\\) and \\(r\\), every term cancels and we obtain  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\,B=0\\,}. \\tag{25}\n\\]\n\n-------------------------------------------